meta {
  name: Delete Product
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against a disposable product created just for
  this test (`sku: "WC-TEST-DISPOSABLE-003"`, id `6aa022d82b6fd055ffb7caa8`,
  since deleted) -- **not** the kept "Create Product - Full Featured.bru"
  fixture.

  `204 No Content` -- matches `API V3.md`'s stated prose convention,
  **not** `openapi_pimv3.json`'s declared `200`. A follow-up `GET` on the
  same id then returns `404`.

  ## Identifier-by-SKU re-confirmed still false
  `GET /products/WC-TEST-FULL-001` (by SKU, on the kept fixture) still
  returns `422` (`Id must be of type PydanticObjectId`) -- same result as
  Phase 0's original finding against a different, pre-existing product.
  `API V3.md`'s claim that this resource specifically supports SKU lookup
  does not hold here either, on a product this session created itself
  (rules out any theory that it only fails for pre-existing/legacy
  products).
}
